WEBVTT

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.410
Where are our shadow masters?

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.540
The rules are simple.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:21.210
You must exit the garden
before the allotted time expires.

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:23.420
But first, you must save your masters.

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:26.300
Save them? What have you done?

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.800
You must be concerned.
It's important to feel that way.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.180
After all, living dolls exist
for the sake of their masters.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.850
Why are you putting us through this?!

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.850
Such questions are trivial, immaterial!

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.440
Consider carefully what you
should be thinking about

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:44.310
and what you should not be.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.690
You must protect your masters,
for they are nobles.

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:52.110
No harm must come to a living doll's
face while in the labyrinth.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.120
And a shadow's attire must not get dirty.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.660
The sootglass takes about two hours
for the soot to go from bottom to top.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:04.500
You must bring your master
to the exit before then.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:09.720
Take this and wait at the entrance
I told each of you to go to.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.560
In the Palm of His Hand

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.560
In the Palm of His Hand

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.560
In the Palm of His Hand

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.560
In the Palm of His Hand

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.560
In the Palm of His Hand

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.560
In the Palm of His Hand

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.560
In the Palm of His Hand

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:51.190
Her dress has been sewn to the chair.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.280
"A flower that causes a rash if touched."

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.580
Each shadow master has been
restrained in a different manner.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.960
What a pleasant surprise.

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.290
I don't even know her name.

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:11.920
We must each go save our own master.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.380
You must wait for Rum to come for you.

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:19.800
Let's go.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:24.520
Talk about creepy.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:28.850
You and Rum hardly ever speak,
but she's a different kind of scary.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.940
You're criticizing a master?

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:35.360
N-No! I meant scary in
a reverential sort of way.

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:37.360
Don't put words in my mouth!

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:41.240
And would you take off that sack already?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.870
It protects my face.
I got the idea from your mask.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.830
Oh, I see.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:53.340
So you're just another one
who only thinks about themself.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.050
You spied Mistress Kate from afar
but didn't stop to help.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.260
Are you done pretending
to be friends with Emilico?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:02.680
Emilico will save Mistress Kate.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.470
Rum will save her own shadow master.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.850
I will save Mistress Louise.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.560
It's that simple.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.610
Damn her. She's unflappable.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:16.400
Mistress Kate told me
I was fine just how I am.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:20.610
And I have no right or
reason to not believe her.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.620
They are all so...

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:27.080
How could I not be the
most outstanding doll of all?

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:30.790
No way I'm losing to the likes of them.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:42.640
Look! There's soot rising into the sky.

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:47.220
Mistress Louise.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:53.400
The soot's gone?

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.480
Where did it go?

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.190
And why'd you think
it was Mistress Louise?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:01.160
All we could see was soot.

00:05:01.160 --> 00:05:05.240
I saw the other shadow
masters in the debut hall.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.910
Mistress Kate's soot goes straight up.

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:10.250
Master John's looks like sparks.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.130
Master Patrick's
spreads in all directions.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:16.460
I couldn't tell with Rum's mistress.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:19.920
Mistress Louise's soot curls.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:24.180
They emit soot in a different
manner? I had no idea.

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:26.260
But she did.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.600
She noticed something
about Patrick before I did.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:33.810
But I don't know why she's gone.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.400
She'd call out to me if she were here.

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.320
After all, Mistress Louise loves me.

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.650
Maybe she's unable to
speak for some reason.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:47.450
That must be it! This must also
be a test for the shadow masters.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.660
But what are <i>they </i>being tested for?

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:54.630
That soot we just saw may have
been an accident, but it drew us here.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:59.760
It indicates that a shadow
master is hidden here.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:03.800
Considering where we've
looked so far, this won't be hard.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.680
After all, shadow masters
emit soot when anxious.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:11.810
It seems you're not here,
so I'll go look elsewhere.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:14.770
No, there <i>is </i>a master here!

00:06:14.770 --> 00:06:17.150
That was on purpose.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:21.320
Mistress Louise can't get
enough of my face and voice.

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:24.320
Enough with all the bragging!

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.780
I, too, have my master's--

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:27.160
No.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:31.750
Simply hearing my voice puts her at ease.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.470
"Make a rope ladder to save her."

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.480
Oh, that was positively horrible!

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:58.980
Lou, how lovely your face is!
Let Louise have a good look!

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:00.520
Hmm? Who is this?

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.610
Ricky. He helped me get here.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:09.120
O lovely Mistress Louise, it is my
pleasure to be at your service.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.290
How repulsive!

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:14.910
You followed Louise's lovely face here?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:19.670
How dare a living doll be attracted to
a shadow's face? You forget your place.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:21.960
No, you have it all wrong.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:25.920
Or perhaps it is Patrick who
is fond of Louise. Is that it?

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:30.350
Well, a pity for you, but we think not.
Patrick is but a minor figure.

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:33.720
The answer is no! No, no, no!

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.350
Lou...

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:40.980
Your work is done here. You may go.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:43.190
How Louise missed her face!

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.240
Let's get a good look at you.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:48.990
How shocking it was to hear
you say you were not here!

00:07:48.990 --> 00:07:52.830
You were relying on Louise's soot
to seek her out, were you not?

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:57.620
Oh, but we must hurry back
to the hall if we are to win!

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:00.960
The fools. They've let their guard down.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:05.050
If I shove them into one of these pits...

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:16.270
This is that dreadful maze
that Master John mentioned.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.440
Let's go!

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.860
S-S-Scorches.

00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.610
Th-There's so many.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:33.700
That gave me goosebumps.

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:36.660
Now's the time to make a you-know-what!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:38.120
A what?

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:45.550
I knew right away that I could make one.

00:08:45.550 --> 00:08:49.550
With my pushcart,
I can collect whatever I need.

00:08:49.550 --> 00:08:53.300
And its handle is perfect
for making a broom!

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:57.930
She didn't choose the pushcart
in order to carry Mistress Kate?!

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:04.820
The bag we received from
Edward gave me another good idea.

00:09:04.820 --> 00:09:09.950
To help Mistress Kate
return to her everyday life,

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.410
I must start by dressing as I always have!

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:16.990
It's a bit awkward, but...

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:21.670
Emilico always has Mistress Kate in mind.

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:25.710
But in my case...

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:30.130
All ready, Rum? We're going in!

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.680
Take that!

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.270
They run if hit from above!

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.150
Now let's try sideways!

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.450
Nice one, Rum!

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.040
Umm...

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.870
Let's take the left path here,

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:03.290
then right at the next branch.

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:07.210
You have a fabulous memory, Rum!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.840
Something's wrong. We've gone too far.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.550
Huh?

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:19.850
There was no path branching right,
or perhaps we missed it.

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.900
Where did we go wrong?

00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:28.360
It's all wrong.

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:30.940
This maze is nothing like the map.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:32.650
The map is probably a lie.

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.910
You really think so?

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:47.250
I'll get rid of the scorches!

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:51.380
Rum, see if you can figure out the map!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:55.220
Emilico is counting on me.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:59.390
But I don't know if I can do it.
Rummy, what do you think?

00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:02.680
There is more to what
Edward said than mere lies.

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:05.350
There must be a hint somewhere.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:06.440
A hint?

00:11:06.440 --> 00:11:12.360
Master John was right about this maze.
It truly is dreadful!

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:16.070
The bridge collapsed after
taking the upper route.

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:21.290
Emilico, look up there.

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.580
It's a hut mark, just like on the map!

00:11:26.580 --> 00:11:31.340
If that's a hut mark up there,
then our current location is...

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:32.920
I figured it out!

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:37.630
It means we are in the lower area
surrounded by walls.

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:40.720
So then this maze doesn't have an exit?

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:45.180
No! "Up" is written
inside of that hut mark!

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:47.520
There must be a way up somewhere!

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:49.310
Let's go find it!

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.690
That tunnel over there goes up.

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:55.570
Let's give it a try!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.620
Look!

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:03.580
That's our way out!

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:05.200
There are more scorches.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.620
They never give up.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:10.710
But I can't use the
broom <i>and </i>hold the cart.

00:12:10.710 --> 00:12:12.090
We can do it.

00:12:12.090 --> 00:12:13.420
Okay!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.170
Here we go!

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.300
Ready, go!

00:12:18.760 --> 00:12:21.010
Hang on!

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:34.780
We did it!

00:12:37.570 --> 00:12:41.410
Oh, look at that.

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:43.620
There's an opening in the hedge.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:47.290
That's a shortcut to Mistress Shirley.

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:49.830
I wonder if it's a trap.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:55.170
I bet Lou did this with her shears!

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:58.800
We're all helping each other
even when we don't know it!

00:12:58.800 --> 00:13:02.050
Now you can go see Mistress Shirley!

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.850
We've been working
as a team the whole time.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:08.810
It's sad to part ways here,

00:13:08.810 --> 00:13:12.150
but you'll get to see
Mistress Shirley again!

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:20.570
Rum! Are you not feeling well?
Have you been hurt?

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:25.740
Once I save Mistress Kate,
maybe I can come help you.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.290
It's not that.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:33.540
Rum isn't Mistress Shirley's face.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:38.170
So then...

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:42.470
who's your true shadow master?

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:48.270
No, what I mean is I'm not Rum!

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:52.140
Y-You're not the real Rum?

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:58.860
Mistress Shirley... never gave me a name.

00:13:59.990 --> 00:14:04.410
We've never even had a conversation.

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.700
After Rummy and I
started talking to each other,

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:11.370
that's when Rummy first called me Rum.

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:14.880
Mistress Shirley doesn't love me.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:19.670
I have no right to even try and save her.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:22.590
I had no idea.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:27.810
Furthermore, I only think about myself.

00:14:27.810 --> 00:14:32.060
You're always thinking about Kate,

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:37.860
but all I ever thought about was how
much I wanted to make it past the debut.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:42.900
I wasn't thinking about Mistress Shirley.

00:14:44.070 --> 00:14:48.160
Mistress Shirley emits next to no soot,

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:51.040
and her room barely needs cleaning.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:54.830
There's nothing for me to do.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.040
I want to make it past the debut,

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:02.210
but maybe Mistress Shirley
doesn't feel the same.

00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:05.760
I can't see her emotions.

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:11.770
That's right. We can't see them.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:16.060
And because we can't see them,
I use my imagination.

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.860
The members of the
Shadows family have it hard.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:24.490
Their soot only expresses
their negative emotions.

00:15:24.490 --> 00:15:29.120
They can't see themselves.
Perhaps that makes them feel anxious.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:33.370
Mistress Kate and I don't
always get along so well.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.460
However...

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:40.210
we don't want to want to increase
the sadness they already feel.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:44.420
So I want to liven things up
by having fun whenever possible!

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:48.140
Now I can't stop thinking
about Mistress Shirley.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:49.890
Let's use our imagination!

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:53.310
Perhaps she's like you
and doesn't like to talk.

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:58.270
And if she doesn't emit much soot,
it might mean she's satisfied with you.

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:04.490
Perhaps she's so obsessed with cleaning
that you never need to clean her room.

00:16:04.490 --> 00:16:09.240
Perhaps she's always trying to
make you laugh by making funny faces.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:13.240
Will I get in trouble
for saying such things?

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:24.510
I want to... make it past the debut...

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:28.680
...with Mistress Shirley!

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.090
After the debut,

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:34.350
we can meet again as Mistress Kate
and Mistress Shirley's faces!

00:16:34.350 --> 00:16:38.940
And I hope you can be
friends with Mistress Kate!

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:45.570
See you soon!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:01.630
One of the chains... broke?

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:03.670
What's going on?

00:17:05.840 --> 00:17:07.550
Another one?

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:10.970
If they all break...

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:15.560
That vent is drawing in the soot.

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:19.520
Were the chains designed to
break as the soot accumulates?

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:22.400
If the soot doesn't stop...

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:24.650
It's no use. There's no stopping it.

00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.730
Controlling the soot

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:30.110
doesn't get rid of
these negative feelings.

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:32.160
Emilico.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:37.290
Mistress Kate!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.710
Emilico?

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.420
It is nearly complete.

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:52.550
This seems a bit excessive,
but it is certainly a fine view.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:56.810
The veiled dolls are out in force.

00:17:59.810 --> 00:18:01.940
Edward.

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:05.980
It's not often one sees
a debut on this scale.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:09.780
Some even end with a
decision made in the debut hall.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:12.990
Ed, this has your personality
written all over it.

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:17.490
This will be quite an enjoyable
debut for the latest candidates,

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:19.870
assuming any <i>can </i>enjoy it.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:25.250
Nothing else matters as long
as this goes according to my plan.

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:28.170
As long as I entertain
those on the third floor

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:31.720
and get Lord Grandfather's attention...

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:35.090
You will ascend to the third floor?

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:39.470
Yet you already have plenty
of power on the second floor.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:44.650
Upon arriving at Lord Grandfather's wing,
I found three different floors,

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:47.480
each with its own ranking.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.150
I must rise straight to the top.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:53.280
Those eminent third-floor figures
don't even send out their faces.

00:18:53.280 --> 00:18:56.450
It's time they open a spot for me.

00:18:56.450 --> 00:18:59.700
You must not speak lightly of such things.

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:01.910
Don't be frightened, Jer.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:04.870
I merely wish to avoid
unnecessary concerns.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.080
Let us proceed with caution.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:12.340
After all, we are the only
three left from our debut.

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:15.840
Should we not pay
attention to the candidates?

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:19.390
Here are the details on all five pairs.

00:19:19.390 --> 00:19:21.350
I've already seen this.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:24.100
On what will you base your decision?

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.520
Information on the soot
and refuse from their rooms

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:28.650
and the Star Bearers' reports.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:31.360
I've decided all of the roles.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:35.240
His potential may very well blossom.

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:37.820
There are outstanding candidates, too.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:40.780
I took that into account
in balancing the game.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:43.500
And this is the one who will fail.

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:47.170
Such limited soot emission
and a meager appetite.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:51.800
And this one? I'm not sure.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:54.210
Seeing this again, they seem so ordinary,

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.220
yet the information is flawless.

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:59.930
It's as if they know
they're being watched.

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.850
Is something the matter, Edward?

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:04.980
No, it's nothing important.

00:20:04.980 --> 00:20:07.730
Aren't you looking forward to the drama?

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:11.360
You already know the answer, Allie.

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:13.900
The answer is no.

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:18.240
Nothing must disturb
the plans for my perfect world.

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:19.990
Indeed.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:23.540
Once again, we simply do
what we always do.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:27.830
Edward, you take point,
and Allie and I provide support.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:32.250
Still, you get to be the face interacting
with those kids on the big stage.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:34.050
I envy you, Ed.

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:39.340
I'd like Lady Aileen and Lord Gerald to
keep the third-floor lords entertained.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:42.550
Spare me your sarcasm.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:04.620
What a truly inane message.

00:21:04.620 --> 00:21:10.040
Barring the path to this plaza
merely spoils the landscape.

00:21:12.380 --> 00:21:15.880
Those dolls I'd taken for dullards--

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:21.550
they keep solving the
clever puzzles I put in their path.

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:07.260
However, Edward has them
all in the palm of his hand!

00:22:08.930 --> 00:22:12.100
What a beautiful melody.

